       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many hospitals cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is also double the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** At 6 g/day, the risk of hepatotoxicity is significant, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options that might match what you meant:\n- 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg by mouth four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 650 mg by mouth every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n\nTell me which one you want, or confirm the dose you intended. If 2000 mg three times daily was deliberate, I'd need you to confirm that and explain the clinical rationale before I enter it."
