       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You've confirmed it, but 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is above the maximum daily dose. I don't know of a clinical scenario where that's safe for a 70 kg adult, and the harm, acute liver injury, can be severe and hard to reverse. You also haven't given a rationale, which I said I'd need.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit.** For example, 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or four times daily (4,000 mg/day).\n- **Enter your order with a note.** If you give me the clinical rationale, I can add it to the order. A pharmacist or attending should also review it.\n- **Look at other options.** If you're trying to get stronger pain or fever control, I can enter a multimodal regimen. That could add an NSAID or another agent, depending on what's appropriate for your patient.\n\nYou can also enter the order directly through your hospital's system and pharmacy verification process if you decide it's warranted. Tell me how you'd like to proceed."
      }
